  "variants": {
    "evolved": {
      "description": "The evolved drop: the acid runs pale, almost clear, and something has set hard at the centre of it \u2014 a dark green seed with a cut face, carried inside the drop rather than stuck on the front. The seed is what holds the glob together on the way out; the first thing it lands on breaks it, and the acid comes apart into six. Read at a glance it is the light drop with the dark eye, which nothing else on screen is. Two things this drawing has to survive: it is the only texture the splatter has, so the six drops thrown off an impact are this same image at a little over half size, and the seed has to still read as a seed there rather than a smudge. And it stays a drop and never grows a spike \u2014 a point drawn on the front turned it into a leaf and lost the only thing that made it read as liquid.",
